<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeno (emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 425–491</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Zeno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zeno was Eastern Roman emperor from 474 to 491, with a break in 475–476 when he was driven out by the usurper Basiliscus. An Isaurian general who married the daughter of Leo I, he received the imperial regalia from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> after the end of the Western empire in 476 and later sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from Odoacer. His Henotikon of 482 tried to settle the disputes over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-chalcedon">Council of Chalcedon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor.jpg" alt="Zeno (emperor)" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Semissis_of_Zeno.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
